# Changelog

## 2026-09-21 — Assembly version stamping in release builds (Issue #23)

- New "Stamp assembly version" step in the shared composite action `.github/actions/build-and-package/action.yml` (between "Restore dependencies" and "Build (Release x64)"): the `release-version` input is validated against `X.Y.Z`/`X.Y.Z-rc.N` (a leading `v` is tolerated, components are capped at 65534) and regex-stamped into the `AssemblyVersion`/`AssemblyFileVersion`/`AssemblyInformationalVersion` attributes of `EmberMediaManager` and `EmberAPI`. SemVer `X.Y.Z` maps to `X.Y.Z.0`, `X.Y.Z-rc.N` to `X.Y.Z.N`; the full SemVer string goes to `AssemblyInformationalVersion`. Stamping stays in the CI working copy (no commit back); an empty `release-version` skips the step.
- The "Verify publish output" step now verifies the stamped artifacts whenever `release-version` is set: `FileVersion`, `AssemblyVersion` and `ProductVersion` of `publish/Ember Media Manager.exe` and `FileVersion`/`AssemblyVersion` of `publish/EmberAPI.dll` are compared against the stamp step's outputs — a silently non-matching regex replace now fails the build instead of shipping an unstamped executable.
- `scripts/resolve-release-version.mjs` rejects manual tags that cannot be mapped onto an assembly version (anything other than `vX.Y.Z`/`vX.Y.Z-rc.N`, or components > 65534) already in the "Resolve release version" step, before the build starts.
- The checked-in placeholders in both `AssemblyInfo.vb` files were lowered from `1.11.1.0` to `0.0.0.0` plus an empty `AssemblyInformationalVersion`, so unstamped local/non-release builds are recognizable ("Version 0.0.0 x64"). Released executables now display the GitHub release version in About/splash/`mnuVersion`, and `dlgVersions` shows matching "Ember Application"/"Ember API" entries.

## 2026-09-21 — Title-based search for movies and TV shows migrated to the TMDb API (Issue #16)

- The title search of the `scraper.Data.IMDB` module no longer parses the broken IMDb HTML pages (`imdb.com/find`, `imdb.com/search/title`). `SearchMovie`/`SearchTVShow` in `clsScrapeIMDB.vb` now query the TMDb API via `TMDbLib` (`SearchMovieAsync`/`SearchTvShowAsync`, up to 3 result pages) and resolve the IMDb ID of each hit (`GetMovieExternalIdsAsync`/`GetTvShowExternalIdsAsync`). Hits without a resolvable IMDb ID are logged and skipped.
- Search results are classified into *Exact Matches* (title matches after year normalization plus matching year) and *Partial Matches*; the former special categories *Popular Titles*, *TV Movie Titles*, *Video Titles* and *Short Titles* are no longer filled and were removed from the IMDb movie search dialog and the module settings (the five `Search*Titles` settings/checkboxes are deprecated — existing entries in `AdvancedSettings.xml` remain inert).
- New `APIKey` setting in the IMDb module settings (movies and TV): a personal TMDb API key can be entered after *Use my own API key*; an empty field falls back to the embedded Ember API key. Persisted per content type via `AdvancedSettings`.
- Source failures are now distinguishable from "no hits": worker errors propagate through a new `Exception` event to the search dialogs, which show a dedicated error node (*The search could not be completed: …*) with mapped reasons (invalid/missing API key, request limit reached, source unreachable) instead of *No Matches Found*; *Manual IMDB Entry* remains usable as fallback. If the detail lookup for a selected entry fails, the entry can still be confirmed (*The details for the selected entry could not be loaded, but the entry can still be used.*).
- The same error handling was added to the `scraper.Data.TMDB` module (`clsScrapeTMDB.vb`): `APIResult.Result` is no longer evaluated blindly (now `GetAwaiter().GetResult()` inside `Try/Catch`), `bwTMDB_RunWorkerCompleted` checks `e.Error`/`e.Cancelled` before accessing `e.Result`, and all three TMDb search dialogs show the same error node instead of hanging in the loading state.
- `TMDbLib` upgraded to 2.3.0 in both modules (highest .NET Framework-compatible release; 3.x targets net8.0+ only) including transitive packages and a `TMDbLib` binding redirect in `EmberMediaManager\App.config`.
- New UI strings 1493–1498 in `EmberAPI\Translations\en-US.xml`. Help documentation updated under `docs/help/scraper/` (description, troubleshooting, user setup, technical flow, business rules; new `installation.md`).

## 2026-09-20 — Requirements analysis: restore title-based IMDb search for movies and TV shows (Issue #8)

- New analysis/requirements document `docs/analysis/issue-8-titelsuche-imdb.md` for the responsible development project — no code changes in this branch.
- Core finding: the title search of the `scraper.Data.IMDB` module (`SearchMovie`/`SearchTVShow` in `clsScrapeIMDB.vb`) is broken because IMDb answers the scraped `/find` and `/search/title` endpoints with an AWS WAF bot challenge (HTTP 202, `x-amzn-waf-action: challenge`, empty body — live-verified) resp. a rebuilt React frontend; the expected markup no longer exists, so the *Search Results* dialog always shows *No Matches Found*. The IMDb detail fetches (`/reference`, `/episodes`, `/releaseinfo`, `/parentalguide`, `/plotsummary`) use the same source and are presumably broken as well.
- Additional finding: at the affected installation the TMDb data scraper also delivers no search hits although both scrapers are enabled — root cause to be narrowed down by the development project (outdated `TMDbLib` 1.9.1 / possibly invalid embedded fallback API key vs. a scrape-order effect where cancelling the first search dialog aborts the whole scrape chain).
- Recommendation documented: migrate the title search to the TMDb API (existing `TMDbLib` infrastructure in `scraper.TMDB.Data`, IMDb-ID mapping via `FindAsync(FindExternalSource.Imdb)`), keep the `SearchResults_Movie`/`SearchResults_TVShow` result contract, deprecate the five `Search*Titles` settings, and make source failures distinguishable from "no hits". OMDb API documented as alternative, undocumented IMDb-internal endpoints as fallback only.
- Help documentation updated: new `docs/help/scraper/troubleshooting.md` describes the defect and the workaround (manual IMDb-ID entry via *Manual IMDB Entry* in the search dialog); `beschreibung.md` gained a "Known defect" limitation note and `index.md` links the new page.

## 2026-09-20 — CI/CD workflow set and Git hooks (Issue #7)

- New local Git hooks under `.githooks/` (activated once per clone via `install-hooks.cmd`/`install-hooks.sh`, which set `core.hooksPath`): `pre-commit` validates localization files via `translation-check.py` (with a `python`/`python3`/`py -3` fallback), and `pre-push` mirrors the CI security gate by scanning `nuget restore` output for NU190[1-4] vulnerability warnings, blocking the push on findings. `.gitattributes` pins LF endings for `.githooks/*` so the shell hooks work under `core.autocrlf=true`.
- New GitHub Actions workflow set under `.github/workflows/` implementing the `feature branch → staging → master` flow: `PR CI for Staging` (NuGet vulnerability gate + `Debug|x86` and `Release|x64` builds, with back-merge detection), `Pre-Release` on `staging` pushes (same gates plus semantic-release version calculation and automatic `vX.Y.Z-rc.N` pre-releases), `Verify PR Source` (PRs to `master` only from `staging`), automated back-merge and draft promotion PRs, a weekly `Security Scan` (Mondays 04:00 UTC), and `Release` (automatic via semantic-release on `master`, manual `v*.*.*` tags, and asset-repair for interrupted runs).
- Two shared composite actions under `.github/actions/`: `security-scan` (NuGet restore + NU190x evaluation + log artifact, blocking via `fail-on-vulnerabilities`) and `build-and-package` (`Release|x64` MSBuild → `release.zip` + `update.json` update manifest).
- semantic-release toolchain added at the repo root (`package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `release.config.js`, `scripts/resolve-release-version.mjs`); versioning follows Conventional Commits, seeded by tag `v1.12.0`. The NSIS installer remains outside the pipeline.
- `Newtonsoft.Json` updated uniformly to 13.0.3 across nine `packages.config` files plus the matching `<HintPath>`/`<Reference Include>` entries and the two remaining `12.0.0.0` binding redirects — fixes NU1903 (GHSA-5crp-9r3c-p9vr) so the blocking security gate starts green.
- Test execution, code-coverage and `dotnet format` gates of the reference pipeline are intentionally dropped (no executable test suite; format tooling not applicable to the legacy project format); the omissions are documented in the workflow comments.
- New README section "Continuous Integration / Git Hooks" and feature documentation under `docs/help/ci-cd/`.

## 2026-09-19 — Make solution compilable (.NET Framework 4.8)

- The missing external project reference `TVDB` was added to the repository as vendored source under `TheTVDBApi/src/TVDB/` (GPL-3.0, `DanCooper/TheTVDBApi`); the solution and both TVDB scraper projects now point to the repo-internal path. The solution is therefore self-contained buildable after a fresh `git clone`.
- All projects were uniformly raised to .NET Framework 4.8; the 4.8 reference assemblies are provided via NuGet (`Microsoft.NETFramework.ReferenceAssemblies.net48` + `Directory.Build.props`/`FrameworkPathOverride`) — no Developer Pack required.
- `.nuget/NuGet.exe` was updated to 6.14.0, restoring the package restore (`nuget restore`) functionality.
- Existing compile errors in the source code were fixed minimally invasively (among others: missing `Enums.ScraperEventType` definition, missing database methods `Delete_Tag`/`Save_Tag_Movie` ported from upstream 1.11.1, outdated `APIXML.CacheXMLs` call, `if exist` guard in the `EmberAPI` PostBuildEvent, invalid `Prefer32Bit` settings in add-on libraries).
- The solution builds without errors in the configurations `Release|x64`, `Release|x86` and `Debug|Any CPU`; build instructions documented in `README.md` and `docs/help/build/`.
- A startup crash on first run was fixed: `Settings.Load()` in `EmberAPI/clsAPISettings.vb` opened `Settings.xml` before the existence check (`FileNotFoundException` on a fresh profile). The reader is now — as in upstream 1.11.1 — only opened inside the `File.Exists` check; a missing `Settings.xml` leads to default settings instead of a crash.

## 2020-05-11 — Mapping Editor (retroactively documented)

- New generic module `generic.EmberCore.Mapping`: dialogs for maintaining the genre, regex and simple mapping lists (`dlgGenreMapping`, `dlgRegexMapping`, `dlgSimpleMapping`).

## 2018-03-13 — Trakt.tv interface (retroactively documented)

- New interface module `generic.Interface.Trakttv`: Trakt account authorization (`frmAuthorize`), sync manager (`dlgTrakttvManager`) for watched state/playcounts in both directions, plus context-menu entries per content type.

## 2015-07-07 — Kodi integration (retroactively documented)

- New C# library `KodiAPI` (`XBMCRPC`): generated JSON-RPC client with method groups `VideoLibrary`, `Files`, `Textures`, `Player` and others, plus WebSocket notifications.
- New interface module `generic.Interface.Kodi`: multi-host management (`dlgHost`), mapping of local Ember paths to Kodi sources and real-time synchronization on `ModuleEventType` events (Edit/Scrape/Remove/Scan/Clean).

## 2015-06-15 — TheTVDB data scraper (retroactively documented)

- New scraper module `scraper.Data.TVDB` for TV show metadata from TheTVDB (uses the TVDB client library).

## 2015-03-08 — Media list editor (retroactively documented)

- New generic module `generic.EmberCore.FilterEditor` (module class `genericMediaListEditor`): editor for custom filters and media lists.

## 2015-03-05 — Tag Manager (retroactively documented)

- New generic module `generic.EmberCore.TagManager`: management of tags/keywords with its own dialog (`dlgTagManager`).

## 2014-04-03 — BuildSetup / Installer (retroactively documented)

- `BuildSetup/` introduced: NSIS installer script (`1.4_InstallerScript.nsi`), build batch files for x86/x64 and helper tools (`BRC32`, `tx`, `txDownload`).

## 2013-09-29 — Trakt.tv API library (retroactively documented)

- New C# library `Trakttv`: Trakt API v2 client with sync endpoints (history, ratings, watchlist, collection, lists, comments), data models and error types.

## 2013-05-17 — Initial project import 1.4.x (retroactively documented)

- Core of the application: `EmberMediaManager` (WinForms main application with `frmMain` and edit/source/settings dialogs) and `EmberAPI` (SQLite database `MyVideos`, scanner, NFO, images, MediaInfo/FFmpeg, settings, module system `ModulesManager` with `GenericModule` and scraper interfaces).
- Scraper modules: data (IMDb, TMDb, OMDb, OFDb, Moviepilot), images (TMDb, Fanart.tv, TVDB), trailers (YouTube, TMDb, Apple, hd-trailers.net, Videobuster), themes (YouTube, TelevisionTunes).
- Generic modules: Bulk Renamer, Movie Exporter, Media File Manager, context menu, metadata editor, video source mapping.
- Scraper design separated by groups (data, images, trailers, themes) with scrape order and central image selection.
